{
 "result": "maze.py is built and adopted. It reads the grid from stdin, pads it with a '#' border so neighbour lookups need no boundary checks, and runs a level-by-level BFS over a flat bytearray, printing the S-to-E distance or -1. It matches all three samples (2008, -1, 78). The bench adopted the padded variant at +28% over the earlier baseline (2.57 to about 3.40 median). I stopped here because the gain is already banked and the remaining ideas are small next to the 4.4% noise floor.",
